From 6adc4d907c75a13d9f29695049251329da08233d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:07:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Chalk engine: narration-driven animated chalkboard
 documentary renderer

Rebuilds the chalkboard mode around a persistent, incremental chalk renderer.

- chalk_engine: grainy chalk on a textured slate board, incremental strokes, camera
  (pans, push-ins, close-ups, drift, impact shake), eraser with ghost smudges, chalk dust
- chalk_lettering: single-line stroke font; text is written stroke by stroke
- chalk_illustrations: 57 procedural drawings in 4 detail stages + SVG path import
- chalk_composer: 12 layouts, word-anchored scheduling, pacing decisions (draw ahead of
  the word, then lose hatching/decoration, only then hurry the pen), camera/transitions
- chalk_story: sentence-aware beats, layout/caption/anchor selection, AI output validation
- chalk_voice + audio.py: Edge TTS word timestamps saved as <audio>.words.json,
  alignment to script words, offline espeak-ng placeholder narration
- chalk_sound: chalk/eraser/impact/whoosh synthesis driven by the drawing program,
  music ducking and swells
- tools/chalk_qa.py, tools/make_chalk_preview.py, docs/chalk_engine.md, 41 new tests

render_chalkboard_video uses the new engine by default; FERN_CHALK_ENGINE=legacy (or a
missing OpenCV) keeps the previous renderer. Adds numpy and opencv-python-headless.
